From 0b1d31e34a09cfee9edafb894a8515270122a805 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CounterStrikeXB2 <cs2@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] video, input: hooks for a title's own presenter and host
 menus; keymap file (CounterStrikeXB2 local patch)

For a project whose GPU renderer draws the frame and that puts its own menus
over the game (Counter-Strike's ESC quit prompt, F1 settings and config.exe):

- fb_present: xbox_FramebufferSetPresenter -- the flip calls the title's
  presenter instead of copying the guest framebuffer into the window (the copy
  is still made under RECOMP_FB_DUMP); the window thread then only pumps
  messages and the toolkit's own D3D presenter is not started on the window.
  xbox_FramebufferSetKeyFilter sees every key message first;
  xbox_FramebufferWindowHwnd; xbox_FramebufferComposeOverlay draws the PVIDEO
  overlay into the caller's frame; xbox_FramebufferToggleFullscreen /
  IsFullscreen from any thread.
- keyboard: RECOMP_KEYMAP=<file> reads a [keys] section ("a = Z, Space", one
  line per control in input_map's names) over the default map, once.
- xinput_device: xbox_InputSetHold -- port 0 reads as neutral while a host
  menu that the pad also drives is open; the game keeps running.
---
